sentences.text:
The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Spl.Case No.1610/2024 pending before the Court of Additional City Civil and Sessions Judge, FTSC-II arising out of Crime No.282/2024 registered by Peenya Police Station, Bengaluru, for the offences punishable under NC: 2024:KHC:51202 Sections 363, 376 of IPC, Section 6 of Sanjay Kumar vs The State Of Karnataka By on 12 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/158179968/
3 Protection of Children from Sexual Ofences Act, 2012 (for shot, 'POCSO') and Sections 9 and 10 of Prohibition of Child Marriage Act, 2006, subject to the following conditions:
a) Petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.1,00,000/- (Rupees One Lakh only) with two sureties for the likesum, to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts his appearance for valid reasons;
c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
d) The petitioner shall not involve in similar offences in future;
 e) The petitioner shall not leave the  jurisdiction of the Trial Court without permission of the said Court until the case registered against him is disposed off.
Sd/-
(S VISHWAJITH SHETTY) JUDGE MKM Sanjay Kumar vs The State Of Karnataka By on 12 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/158179968/
